WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.090
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.360 --> 01:34.950
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.289 --> 01:37.820
[Episode 19]

4
01:38.310 --> 01:40.720
Yesterday, someone

5
01:40.820 --> 01:43.350
[Bo Gu (Qin Bangxian), Head of the CPC Central Committee]

6
01:42.460 --> 01:43.770
called me a traitor.

7
01:43.410 --> 01:47.780
[Mao Zedong Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

8
01:44.460 --> 01:45.380
I was afraid of

9
01:45.820 --> 01:47.940
being branded one.

10
01:47.960 --> 01:50.039
[Li De, Military Adviser of the Communist International]

11
01:48.460 --> 01:50.180
How could I answer to the Comintern?

12
01:50.180 --> 01:52.030
[Li Fuchun, Acting Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

13
01:50.460 --> 01:52.390
How could I face Comrade Wang Ming?

14
01:52.770 --> 01:54.050
This concerns

15
01:54.050 --> 01:55.350
fundamental principles of our political line.

16
01:55.350 --> 01:56.240
Comrades.

17
01:57.690 --> 02:00.290
Who could possibly bear that responsibility?

18
02:00.300 --> 02:01.330
Comrade Bo Gu,

19
02:01.690 --> 02:03.820
we share the same revolutionary ideals.

20
02:03.820 --> 02:05.130
We have always stood united

21
02:05.130 --> 02:06.020
in opposing imperialism

22
02:06.020 --> 02:08.090
and Chiang Kai-shek's

23
02:08.419 --> 02:09.750
reactionary Kuomintang regime.

24
02:09.750 --> 02:10.690
So please don't let this weigh so heavily

25
02:10.690 --> 02:12.180
on your mind.

26
02:12.860 --> 02:14.140
Today's meeting

27
02:14.140 --> 02:15.420
is about the issue, not the person.

28
02:15.370 --> 02:17.910
[Wang Jiaxiang Alternate Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee Vice Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

29
02:16.050 --> 02:17.050
Comrade Bo Gu,

30
02:17.380 --> 02:20.590
I listened to what you said about

31
02:21.490 --> 02:22.810
your original intentions before the meeting,

32
02:22.810 --> 02:24.300
and I believe everyone else did, too.

33
02:23.880 --> 02:26.420
[Liu Bocheng, Chief of the General Staff of the Red Army and concurrently Commander of the Military Commission Column]

34
02:25.020 --> 02:26.420
if I remember correctly,

35
02:26.579 --> 02:29.090
you joined the Party in 1925,

36
02:26.610 --> 02:28.990
[Liu Shaoqi Alternate Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee CPC Central Representative to the 5th Red Army Corps]

37
02:29.300 --> 02:30.530
when you were just 18.

38
02:31.260 --> 02:32.700
Before a year had passed,

39
02:33.050 --> 02:34.050
you were sent to Moscow

40
02:34.050 --> 02:35.430
to study.

41
02:35.490 --> 02:38.540
[Chen Yun, Member of the Standing Committee of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee and Political Commissar of the Military Commission Column]

42
02:36.020 --> 02:37.550
You returned to China at 23,

43
02:37.640 --> 02:38.710
and just over a year later,

44
02:38.710 --> 02:40.510
Comrade Wang Ming appointed you

45
02:41.650 --> 02:43.270
to lead the Central Committee.

46
02:43.270 --> 02:45.430
[Zhu De, Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission, Commander-in-Chief of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

47
02:43.900 --> 02:46.260
Your political and theoretical acumen,

48
02:46.650 --> 02:48.090
your intelligence and determination,

49
02:48.090 --> 02:50.320
and your courage and passion for the revolution

50
02:50.320 --> 02:52.180
are all there for everyone to see.

51
02:53.610 --> 02:54.420
Chairman Mao,

52
02:54.579 --> 02:56.020
then tell us about Comrade Bo Gu's

53
02:55.030 --> 02:57.640
[Lin Biao, Commander of the 1st Red Army Corps]

54
02:56.940 --> 02:58.060
shortcomings.

55
03:00.730 --> 03:01.730
We've all been

56
03:02.800 --> 03:04.310
speaking frankly today,

57
03:04.910 --> 03:06.790
so let me be frank, too.

58
03:07.090 --> 03:08.890
Is that all right, Comrade Bo Gu?

59
03:10.380 --> 03:12.040
I'll listen with an open mind.

60
03:12.420 --> 03:13.260
I think

61
03:13.490 --> 03:15.050
Comrade Bo Gu's main weakness

62
03:15.050 --> 03:17.770
is that he's focused on the bigger picture

63
03:18.180 --> 03:21.490
but has lost sight of China's realities here and now.

64
03:22.020 --> 03:25.329
On top of that, he lacks practical political experience

65
03:23.690 --> 03:25.420
[Kaifeng (He Kewen) Alternate Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee CPC Central Committee Representative to the 9th Red Army Corps]

66
03:25.530 --> 03:27.370
and has no experience commanding troops.

67
03:27.370 --> 03:30.140
So politically, he has to follow Wang Ming,

68
03:30.400 --> 03:33.030
and militarily, he has to follow Li De.

69
03:33.460 --> 03:35.700
He really has little choice but to do as they say.

70
03:35.700 --> 03:37.140
At the same time,

71
03:37.260 --> 03:39.520
he needs to establish his own authority.

72
03:39.550 --> 03:41.240
So he becomes more autocratic

73
03:41.340 --> 03:42.800
and quick to brand anyone who disagrees with him

74
03:42.800 --> 03:44.810
[Deng Xiaoping, Secretary-General of the CPC Central Committee]

75
03:43.050 --> 03:44.930
as a problem to be dealt with.

76
03:45.490 --> 03:46.579
Over time,

77
03:47.530 --> 03:50.190
this has led to the mistakes we're seeing today.

78
03:51.380 --> 03:53.820
Comrade Zedong, I really didn't expect

79
03:52.310 --> 03:55.590
[Zhou Enlai, CPC Central Committee Politburo Standing Committee, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission, General Political Commissar of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

80
03:54.530 --> 03:57.790
you to have such a profound understanding of Comrade Bo Gu.

81
03:58.210 --> 03:59.860
Only when the pain has passed

82
04:02.180 --> 04:04.810
can one truly reflect on what it was like to suffer.

83
04:04.810 --> 04:07.050
Our Communist Party has come a long way,

84
04:07.420 --> 04:09.460
and the revolutionary cause has never been easy.

85
04:09.460 --> 04:11.490
If we can't correct our own mistakes

86
04:11.510 --> 04:13.260
in times of adversity

87
04:14.140 --> 04:16.380
or find the courage to take responsibility,

88
04:16.380 --> 04:18.209
we'll never accomplish anything great.

89
04:18.209 --> 04:19.339
Comrade Mao Zedong,

90
04:19.600 --> 04:22.310
thank you for your fair assessment of me.

91
04:23.830 --> 04:26.830
My evaluation and analysis are inevitably biased.

92
04:27.340 --> 04:29.270
As the saying goes, time will tell.

93
04:30.090 --> 04:30.940
Comrade Bo Gu,

94
04:31.290 --> 04:32.290
we're comrades

95
04:32.460 --> 04:33.770
and fellow revolutionaries.

96
04:33.770 --> 04:35.730
There is still a long way to go.

97
04:38.330 --> 04:39.460
Comrades.

98
04:39.970 --> 04:41.770
Comrade Zedong's remarks today

99
04:42.020 --> 04:43.260
have once again shown that

100
04:43.260 --> 04:44.580
our debate

101
04:44.650 --> 04:46.180
is for the good of the Party,

102
04:46.620 --> 04:47.940
just as our unity is.

103
04:47.960 --> 04:52.220
And behind it all, we must learn to bear with one another for the Party's sake.

104
04:52.940 --> 04:54.740
Does anyone have any objections

105
04:54.850 --> 04:56.530
to my proposal that Comrade Mao Zedong

106
04:56.530 --> 04:58.850
return to the Red Army

107
04:59.170 --> 05:00.850
and take command?

108
05:01.940 --> 05:02.230
No.

109
05:02.260 --> 05:02.900
No. No.

110
05:02.970 --> 05:03.460
No.

111
05:03.460 --> 05:05.940
I agree that Comrade Mao Zedong should command the Red Army.

112
05:05.940 --> 05:07.180
I agree.

113
05:07.200 --> 05:09.400
-I second that. -I second that.

114
05:09.430 --> 05:10.400
I disagree.

115
05:14.520 --> 05:16.650
I'm deeply moved

116
05:16.730 --> 05:18.140
by the trust you and everyone else have placed in me

117
05:18.140 --> 05:21.060
But even I, Mao Zedong, can't guarantee

118
05:21.260 --> 05:24.260
that I'll lead the Red Army to victory every time.

119
05:24.650 --> 05:26.250
I've suffered defeats, too.

120
05:26.290 --> 05:28.140
The Battle of Changsha in 1930

121
05:28.500 --> 05:29.770
cost us dearly,

122
05:30.330 --> 05:32.260
and we never managed to take the city.

123
05:32.260 --> 05:33.210
In the 1931

124
05:33.460 --> 05:34.659
Battle of Gaoxingxu,

125
05:34.950 --> 05:37.630
we lost two Red Army division commanders,

126
05:37.830 --> 05:39.220
Zeng Shi'e and Zou Ping.

127
05:39.970 --> 05:41.380
That was a defeat, too.

128
05:41.850 --> 05:43.510
In the 1932 Shuikou Campaign,

129
05:43.700 --> 05:45.530
we eventually took Shuikou,

130
05:45.700 --> 05:48.540
but our casualties were heavy. I'd count that as a defeat as well.

131
05:48.540 --> 05:49.770
Let me make a suggestion.

132
05:49.770 --> 05:50.650
I believe

133
05:51.020 --> 05:53.480
the Red Army should remain under the command

134
05:54.210 --> 05:55.530
of Commander-in-Chief Zhu De

135
05:55.530 --> 05:57.700
and Political Commissar Zhou Enlai.

136
05:58.060 --> 05:59.060
I'll offer advice

137
05:59.530 --> 06:01.390
and help you work out strategies.

138
06:01.400 --> 06:02.990
And it shouldn't be just me, Mao Zedong.

139
06:02.990 --> 06:04.350
Every comrade here

140
06:04.380 --> 06:06.040
can help Commander-in-Chief

141
06:06.100 --> 06:08.560
and Comrade Enlai with advice and strategy.

142
06:08.900 --> 06:11.290
I told Comrades Luofu and Jiaxiang

143
06:10.060 --> 06:11.580
[Luofu (Zhang Wenfu), Member of the Political Bureau Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee; Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

144
06:11.850 --> 06:14.460
that three cobblers together can outsmart Zhuge Liang.

145
06:14.460 --> 06:15.990
With over twenty of us here,

146
06:16.290 --> 06:17.750
we should be worth at least

147
06:18.210 --> 06:19.740
six and a half Zhuge Liangs!

148
06:20.500 --> 06:21.790
Six and a half Zhuge Liangs.

149
06:21.790 --> 06:23.460
And that's not counting

150
06:23.460 --> 06:24.900
all our excellent commanders and fighters

151
06:24.900 --> 06:26.410
and the experience they've accumulated.

152
06:26.410 --> 06:28.060
A company has over a hundred men.

153
06:28.060 --> 06:29.260
Just do the math!

154
06:29.500 --> 06:30.610
How many Zhuge Liangs does that give us?

155
06:30.610 --> 06:32.080
How could we not win?

156
06:36.960 --> 06:39.230
Comrades, I'd also like to propose

157
06:39.820 --> 06:41.730
that Comrade Mao Zedong

158
06:41.940 --> 06:45.840
be elected to the Standing Committee of the Central Political Bureau.

159
06:45.840 --> 06:48.000
I nominate Comrade Mao Zedong

160
06:48.820 --> 06:51.900
for the Standing Committee of the Central Political Bureau.

161
06:51.900 --> 06:54.700
I support Comrade Mao Zedong's election

162
06:54.770 --> 06:56.260
to the Standing Committee of the Central Political Bureau.

163
06:56.260 --> 06:57.409
I agree.

164
06:57.650 --> 06:59.170
-I second that. -I second that.

165
06:59.170 --> 07:01.020
-I second that. -I second that.

166
07:08.970 --> 07:09.900
Comrades,

167
07:10.330 --> 07:11.530
before this meeting,

168
07:12.260 --> 07:14.650
I asked myself a question:

169
07:15.020 --> 07:16.850
What kind of people

170
07:17.090 --> 07:19.460
does China need today?

171
07:20.090 --> 07:21.330
And what kind of people should we,

172
07:21.330 --> 07:23.730
the CPC and the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army

173
07:23.730 --> 07:25.730
under its leadership, strive to be?

174
07:26.020 --> 07:26.730
I think

175
07:26.940 --> 07:28.970
first and foremost, we must be people

176
07:28.970 --> 07:30.400
who stand tall and face the world with pride

177
07:30.400 --> 07:31.950
and confidence.

178
07:32.820 --> 07:33.880
Every one of us here

179
07:33.970 --> 07:35.900
should strive to be that kind of person.

180
07:35.900 --> 07:38.700
Only when we stand tall and believe in ourselves

181
07:39.060 --> 07:41.290
can we move forward with confidence.

182
07:41.580 --> 07:43.540
Only by moving forward with confidence

183
07:43.540 --> 07:45.970
can we overcome one difficulty after another.

184
07:45.970 --> 07:46.850
Only by overcoming

185
07:46.850 --> 07:48.500
one difficulty after another

186
07:48.500 --> 07:50.360
can we achieve complete victory.

187
07:50.970 --> 07:53.530
We Chinese have never been afraid of difficulties

188
07:53.530 --> 07:54.409
or brute force.

189
07:54.820 --> 07:55.900
Yu the Great taming the floods,

190
07:55.900 --> 07:56.970
to Yu Gong who moved mountains

191
07:56.970 --> 07:58.330
and Jingwei who tried to fill the sea,

192
07:58.330 --> 07:59.590
our people have always

193
07:59.820 --> 08:00.970
had the courage

194
08:01.620 --> 08:02.940
to face the impossible

195
08:03.070 --> 08:05.600
and the tenacity to overcome every obstacle.

196
08:05.710 --> 08:06.540
Comrades,

197
08:06.910 --> 08:08.260
fellow revolutionaries,

198
08:08.260 --> 08:10.460
China's greatest crisis today

199
08:11.210 --> 08:12.900
comes from foreign aggression.

200
08:12.900 --> 08:13.870
Japanese imperialism

201
08:13.870 --> 08:16.130
has advanced from the Northeast into North China,

202
08:16.130 --> 08:18.860
and its forces have even attacked us in Shanghai.

203
08:19.090 --> 08:20.260
This is a matter

204
08:20.500 --> 08:23.170
of life and death for our nation.

205
08:24.060 --> 08:25.260
Let us not forget that

206
08:25.410 --> 08:26.580
since Britain

207
08:26.830 --> 08:28.340
invaded China in 1840,

208
08:28.690 --> 08:30.300
we have never won a war

209
08:30.330 --> 08:31.700
against a foreign power.

210
08:31.700 --> 08:33.470
Every time, we have suffered defeat,

211
08:33.470 --> 08:34.929
signed unequal treaties,

212
08:35.020 --> 08:36.260
surrendered territory, paid indemnities,

213
08:36.260 --> 08:38.409
and endured national humiliation.

214
08:38.860 --> 08:40.020
And let us not forget

215
08:40.289 --> 08:41.530
that even today,

216
08:41.590 --> 08:43.450
Chiang Kai-shek still invokes the slogan,

217
08:43.450 --> 08:45.510
"Pacify the country before resisting foreign aggression."

218
08:45.510 --> 08:47.170
He makes concessions to Japan

219
08:48.160 --> 08:50.810
while relentlessly seeking to wipe out the Red Army.

220
08:50.810 --> 08:53.620
If the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army, under the leadership of the CPC,

221
08:53.620 --> 08:56.450
can't even defeat

222
08:56.470 --> 08:57.770
the Kuomintang forces,

223
08:57.770 --> 09:00.670
how can we hope to lead the fight against Japanese aggression?

224
09:00.670 --> 09:02.500
If we can't lead the Chinese people

225
09:02.500 --> 09:03.760
to victory in this war,

226
09:04.220 --> 09:07.360
if we can't help them break free

227
09:07.390 --> 09:09.690
from a century of invasion and oppression,

228
09:09.690 --> 09:11.530
then we have no right to speak of ideals.

229
09:11.530 --> 09:13.110
That was never our original purpose,

230
09:13.110 --> 09:14.830
nor is it the future we strive for.

231
09:14.830 --> 09:15.980
From the day

232
09:16.170 --> 09:17.340
it was founded,

233
09:17.700 --> 09:19.230
the CPC has been determined

234
09:19.260 --> 09:21.390
to lead China toward a brighter future

235
09:21.620 --> 09:22.950
and build a society

236
09:23.020 --> 09:25.150
where the people can live happy lives.

237
09:25.620 --> 09:27.620
We have fought for this for 14 years,

238
09:27.620 --> 09:28.980
and as a result, we have suffered

239
09:28.980 --> 09:31.260
various suppressions and encirclements.

240
09:31.260 --> 09:32.920
But we have never backed down,

241
09:33.450 --> 09:35.380
nor have we ever stopped fighting.

242
09:35.740 --> 09:37.290
Some comrades have sacrificed their lives,

243
09:37.290 --> 09:39.770
and the remaining comrades have stepped into the breach

244
09:39.770 --> 09:40.860
and forged ahead.

245
09:41.050 --> 09:42.220
What has kept us going?

246
09:42.220 --> 09:44.690
It's the faith we carry in our hearts.

247
09:45.340 --> 09:48.530
It's the confidence of the Chinese people in themselves.

248
09:48.530 --> 09:51.260
Today, we are correcting the mistakes of the past

249
09:51.570 --> 09:52.570
to uphold

250
09:52.570 --> 09:54.050
the truth of Marxism.

251
09:54.690 --> 09:56.100
China needs Marxism

252
09:56.380 --> 09:57.840
to solve its own problems,

253
09:58.020 --> 09:59.050
and Marxism

254
09:59.260 --> 10:01.530
needs China to prove

255
10:01.810 --> 10:03.410
that it is a universal truth.

256
10:03.900 --> 10:05.300
Comrade Luofu once said,

257
10:05.530 --> 10:06.990
"Wherever the truth lies,

258
10:07.290 --> 10:08.730
that's where we should stand."

259
10:08.730 --> 10:09.990
I couldn't agree more.

260
10:11.020 --> 10:12.930
But where does the truth lie?

261
10:14.140 --> 10:16.730
It lies with Chinese revolutionaries

262
10:16.760 --> 10:19.130
who understand China's realities.

263
10:19.930 --> 10:22.070
It lies along the Red Army's westward march.

264
10:22.070 --> 10:25.400
It lies beneath the feet of our Red Army soldiers.

265
10:26.620 --> 10:29.190
It is up to us Chinese revolutionaries

266
10:29.450 --> 10:32.050
to forge a path to the truth with our own feet

267
10:32.370 --> 10:34.230
and light the way with our hearts.

268
10:35.020 --> 10:36.020
We firmly believe

269
10:36.220 --> 10:38.450
that we Chinese can stand tall,

270
10:39.050 --> 10:40.290
hold our heads high,

271
10:40.450 --> 10:43.740
and face every challenge with confidence.

272
10:44.570 --> 10:45.830
The future of our Party

273
10:45.860 --> 10:47.020
and of China

274
10:47.290 --> 10:50.930
will always be bright and full of promise.

275
11:10.860 --> 11:11.790
I hereby declare

276
11:12.050 --> 11:14.380
the motion to add Comrade Mao Zedong

277
11:14.860 --> 11:17.620
to the Standing Committee of the Central Political Bureau

278
11:17.620 --> 11:18.750
officially passed.

279
11:22.150 --> 11:24.480
On January 17, 1935,

280
11:24.810 --> 11:27.450
the three-day Zunyi Conference came to a close.

281
11:27.450 --> 11:28.690
The meeting decided to

282
11:28.690 --> 11:31.980
add Mao Zedong to the Standing Committee of the Central Political Bureau

283
11:31.980 --> 11:34.770
and appointed Zhang Wentian to draft the conference resolution.

284
11:34.770 --> 11:36.220
After review by the Standing Committee,

285
11:36.220 --> 11:38.150
it would be circulated to Party branches for discussion.

286
11:38.150 --> 11:41.050
The conference also dissolved the "Troika" formed before the Long March.

287
11:41.050 --> 11:42.690
Zhu De and Zhou Enlai, the Commander-in-Chief,

288
11:42.690 --> 11:45.740
would continue to direct military operations,

289
11:45.900 --> 11:48.220
with Zhou Enlai entrusted by the Party

290
11:48.220 --> 11:49.690
to make the final decisions

291
11:49.690 --> 11:52.050
on military command.

292
11:52.980 --> 11:54.460
After the conference, Mao Zedong

293
11:54.460 --> 11:56.000
was assigned to assist Zhou Enlai

294
11:56.000 --> 11:58.170
with military command.

295
11:59.620 --> 12:00.810
The Zunyi Conference

296
12:00.810 --> 12:02.690
was a decisive turning point

297
12:02.690 --> 12:05.380
in the history of the CPC, one on which the Party's very survival depended.

298
12:05.380 --> 12:06.380
The conference was held at a critical moment,

299
12:06.380 --> 12:08.930
following the Red Army's failure in its Counter-Encirclement Campaign

300
12:08.930 --> 12:10.100
and its severe setbacks

301
12:10.100 --> 12:12.700
in the early stages of the Long March.

302
12:13.020 --> 12:15.570
It effectively established Comrade Mao Zedong's leadership

303
12:15.570 --> 12:18.370
in the Party's Central Committee and the Red Army,

304
12:18.770 --> 12:19.770
began to establish

305
12:19.770 --> 12:22.170
the leading position

306
12:22.290 --> 12:24.300
within the Central Committee of the correct Marxist line

307
12:24.300 --> 12:26.500
represented primarily by Comrade Mao,

308
12:26.560 --> 12:29.740
and marked the emergence of the Party's first generation of central leadership,

309
12:29.740 --> 12:31.780
with Comrade Mao Zedong at its core.

310
12:31.900 --> 12:34.340
The conference ushered in a new stage in which the Party

311
12:34.340 --> 12:37.760
independently addressed the practical problems of the Chinese revolution.

312
12:37.760 --> 12:39.450
At the most critical juncture,

313
12:39.450 --> 12:41.660
it saved the Party, saved the Red Army,

314
12:41.810 --> 12:43.740
and saved the Chinese revolution,

315
12:43.770 --> 12:47.770
laying the foundation for the successful completion of the Long March.

316
12:50.090 --> 12:56.450
[Nanjing]

317
13:06.640 --> 13:08.050
[Yan Daogang, Director of the Aide-de-Camp Office of the Generalissimo of the Military Affairs Commission of the Nationalist Government]

318
13:06.850 --> 13:07.980
Everyone, I'm sorry

319
13:08.000 --> 13:09.240
for keeping you waiting.

320
13:08.120 --> 13:10.140
[Yang Yongtai, Secretary of Nanchang Headquarters]

321
13:09.650 --> 13:11.620
I don't know what's going on lately.

322
13:10.240 --> 13:13.380
[Chiang Kai-shek, Generalissimo of the Military Affairs of the Commission of Kuomintang]

323
13:13.020 --> 13:14.450
I've been having nightmares.

324
13:14.450 --> 13:15.380
Generalissimo,

325
13:15.380 --> 13:17.860
you've been pushing yourself too hard lately.

326
13:17.860 --> 13:19.100
Why don't you go back

327
13:19.100 --> 13:20.360
and get some solid rest?

328
13:20.360 --> 13:21.350
How can I rest?

329
13:22.620 --> 13:25.150
Internal troubles threaten to bring us down,

330
13:25.460 --> 13:28.190
while foreign aggression looms like a tiger on the prowl.

331
13:28.190 --> 13:30.470
How could any of this not wear me down?

332
13:30.570 --> 13:33.500
[Chen Cheng Commander-in-Chief of the Kuomintang Army's Reserve Forces in Jiangxi]

333
13:32.450 --> 13:33.380
Generalissimo,

334
13:34.320 --> 13:35.610
negotiations over the Chahar Incident

335
13:35.610 --> 13:37.130
are already underway.

336
13:37.150 --> 13:38.750
We should have a result soon.

337
13:39.290 --> 13:40.950
I'm afraid Japan's ambitions

338
13:41.290 --> 13:42.530
go far beyond that.

339
13:43.020 --> 13:44.770
They want all of North China.

340
13:45.540 --> 13:47.690
Although the Japanese are being aggressive,

341
13:47.690 --> 13:50.540
they're still testing the waters by provoking incidents.

342
13:50.540 --> 13:53.100
If our negotiators handle things skillfully,

343
13:53.100 --> 13:54.130
Japan may not take further action

344
13:54.130 --> 13:56.090
in the near future.

345
13:58.210 --> 13:58.880
Zurong,

346
13:59.040 --> 13:59.960
where's the "Plan for Encirclement and Suppression South of the Yangtze"

347
13:59.960 --> 14:01.480
I asked you to bring?

348
14:07.170 --> 14:08.230
Please take a look.

349
14:11.270 --> 14:12.230
Our overall plan

350
14:12.440 --> 14:15.260
is to combine the forces of Hunan, Sichuan, Yunnan, Guizhou,

351
14:15.260 --> 14:16.460
and the Central Army,

352
14:16.500 --> 14:17.690
a total of 400,000 troops,

353
14:17.690 --> 14:20.170
to hem in the Communist army in northern Guizhou

354
14:20.170 --> 14:21.710
and annihilate them together.

355
14:21.710 --> 14:24.110
But what is the Communist army's next move?

356
14:24.310 --> 14:25.640
Will they cross north into Sichuan,

357
14:25.640 --> 14:26.970
flee east into Hunan,

358
14:27.130 --> 14:28.660
or escape west into Yunnan?

359
14:28.690 --> 14:30.690
We should have some foresight.

360
14:32.040 --> 14:34.250
If I had to pick a direction,

361
14:34.530 --> 14:35.410
I think

362
14:35.530 --> 14:37.780
Zhu De and Mao Zedong are most likely to cross the Yangtze north

363
14:37.780 --> 14:40.900
into Sichuan and join forces with Xu Xiangqian's troops.

364
14:40.900 --> 14:41.960
What is your basis?

365
14:42.190 --> 14:44.920
My assessment isn't based on the Communist army,

366
14:44.930 --> 14:46.140
but on Liu Xiang.

367
14:46.630 --> 14:48.020
He Guoguang's telegram says rumors

368
14:48.020 --> 14:48.930
have been running rampant in Chongqing these past few days

369
14:48.930 --> 14:51.530
that the Communist army is heading for Sichuan,

370
14:51.530 --> 14:53.290
throwing the whole city into a panic.

371
14:53.290 --> 14:55.530
Many wealthy families are relocating,

372
14:55.770 --> 14:57.980
and there's even been a bank run.

373
14:58.170 --> 14:59.980
Liu Xiang is beside himself with worry.

374
14:59.980 --> 15:01.770
If Liu Xiang weren't worried,

375
15:02.100 --> 15:04.120
the Sichuan Army wouldn't move south out of the province.

376
15:04.120 --> 15:05.410
And if they don't come out,

377
15:05.410 --> 15:07.010
how are we supposed to get in?

378
15:07.380 --> 15:10.310
Then we should make sure everyone believes

379
15:10.410 --> 15:12.200
Zhu and Mao's forces are planning

380
15:12.200 --> 15:13.250
to cross the Yangtze into Sichuan.

381
15:13.250 --> 15:14.130
In my opinion,

382
15:14.620 --> 15:16.740
Liu Xiang can't afford to lose.

383
15:24.130 --> 15:28.540
[Chongqing]

384
15:32.170 --> 15:33.570
Director He has arrived.

385
15:35.140 --> 15:35.780
Excuse me.

386
15:35.380 --> 15:37.940
[Guo Xunqi Brigade Commander of the Third Brigade, Sichuan Army Training Division]

387
15:36.440 --> 15:38.090
Brother, thank you for your hard work.

388
15:38.090 --> 15:39.790
[He Guoguang Director of the Headquarters Staff Regiment of the Chairman's Field Headquarters, National Military Council of the Kuomintang Government]

389
15:38.860 --> 15:41.460
Everyone is here. Thank you for your hard work.

390
15:41.530 --> 15:42.770
Thank you for your hard work, everyone.

391
15:42.770 --> 15:44.240
Thank you for your hard work, everyone.

392
15:44.240 --> 15:46.700
Brother Yizhi, thank you for your hard work.

393
15:47.810 --> 15:48.860
Director He,

394
15:49.690 --> 15:50.890
you are the superior.

395
15:51.530 --> 15:53.390
You should take the seat of honor.

396
15:54.060 --> 15:55.520
There is a seat over there.

397
15:57.100 --> 15:57.740
Come.

398
15:59.220 --> 16:00.140
Let me see.

399
16:00.940 --> 16:03.670
Why didn't you bring out this good stuff earlier?

400
16:05.100 --> 16:07.300
You should have brought it out earlier.

401
16:13.410 --> 16:15.540
The Commander-in-Chief has arrived!

402
16:30.740 --> 16:31.800
Brother Yuanjing,

403
16:32.810 --> 16:33.540
come and sit.

404
16:33.600 --> 16:35.220
Chairman Liu, no need.

405
16:35.440 --> 16:36.140
It's well-ventilated here,

406
16:36.140 --> 16:36.860
nice and cool.

407
16:36.800 --> 16:38.640
[Liu Xiang, Chief Commander of Sichuan "Extermination of Communist"]

408
16:36.900 --> 16:38.050
This is improper. Come.

409
16:38.050 --> 16:38.810
No need.

410
16:41.260 --> 16:41.980
Sit.

411
16:45.620 --> 16:46.290
Everyone,

412
16:46.730 --> 16:49.330
do you know why I moved the suppression headquarters

413
16:49.330 --> 16:51.440
from Chengdu to Chongqing?

414
16:53.410 --> 16:54.410
It's because

415
16:55.300 --> 16:58.450
Generalissimo Chiang moved his military advisory group

416
16:58.450 --> 16:59.650
to Chongqing.

417
17:00.960 --> 17:03.480
Do you know why Generalissimo Chiang did this?

418
17:03.480 --> 17:05.520
It shows just how much importance

419
17:05.960 --> 17:09.550
he places on Sichuan.

420
17:10.520 --> 17:11.579
Brother Yuanjing,

421
17:12.770 --> 17:13.940
am I right?

422
17:15.410 --> 17:17.339
Yes, absolutely right.

423
17:18.800 --> 17:21.410
Generalissimo Chiang couldn't possibly

424
17:21.430 --> 17:22.829
care more about Sichuan.

425
17:23.410 --> 17:25.339
But I believe

426
17:25.900 --> 17:28.450
the Communist soldiers

427
17:28.480 --> 17:29.850
care even more.

428
17:30.770 --> 17:33.040
Director He, if you have something to say, just say it.

429
17:33.040 --> 17:34.350
Don't be sarcastic.

430
17:34.890 --> 17:37.520
Brother Yizhi, you misunderstood me.

431
17:38.440 --> 17:39.070
Everyone,

432
17:39.520 --> 17:41.850
our Sichuan is known as the Land of Abundance.

433
17:41.850 --> 17:43.720
The Chengdu Plain and the Sichuan-Chongqing area

434
17:43.720 --> 17:45.120
are even more prosperous.

435
17:45.120 --> 17:46.800
As for Zhu and Mao's Communist soldiers,

436
17:46.800 --> 17:47.940
our armies have been chasing and encircling them

437
17:47.940 --> 17:50.170
all the way

438
17:50.300 --> 17:51.210
from Jiangxi

439
17:51.800 --> 17:53.000
to northern Guizhou.

440
17:53.210 --> 17:54.560
Life in Jiangxi

441
17:54.580 --> 17:56.700
was at least bearable,

442
17:56.970 --> 17:58.170
but northern Guizhou

443
17:58.520 --> 18:00.960
is barren,

444
18:00.980 --> 18:02.440
with little food to be had.

445
18:02.450 --> 18:03.580
They're desperate.

446
18:03.830 --> 18:04.960
They want to go back,

447
18:05.030 --> 18:06.140
but they can't.

448
18:06.420 --> 18:07.910
If they want to go east to Hunan,

449
18:07.910 --> 18:09.060
the Hunan Army is blocking them.

450
18:09.060 --> 18:10.860
To the west, the Yunnan Army is blocking them.

451
18:10.860 --> 18:11.690
To the south,

452
18:11.820 --> 18:15.300
there is the natural barrier of the Wujiang River and Xue Yue's Central Army.

453
18:15.300 --> 18:16.300
Brother Fucheng,

454
18:17.200 --> 18:19.390
if you were the Commander-in-Chief of the Communist army,

455
18:19.390 --> 18:20.740
what would you do?

456
18:26.210 --> 18:27.210
It's not hard.

457
18:28.040 --> 18:30.170
Cross the Yangtze into Sichuan

458
18:30.370 --> 18:32.740
and enjoy the rice in Sichuan.

459
18:35.620 --> 18:36.900
Director He, are you saying

460
18:36.900 --> 18:39.710
that our Sichuan Army can't hold the natural barrier of the Yangtze River?

461
18:39.710 --> 18:42.040
The natural barrier of the Yangtze River?

462
18:44.210 --> 18:47.920
How does the natural barrier of the Yangtze River compare to the Wujiang River and the Xiang River?

463
18:47.920 --> 18:49.140
And how does the Sichuan Army

464
18:49.140 --> 18:51.670
compare with the Guangxi Army and Hunan Army?

465
18:51.670 --> 18:54.330
If Zhu and Mao's Red Army really want to go north,

466
18:54.410 --> 18:57.300
can Xu Xiangqian's forces afford not to come to their aid?

467
18:57.300 --> 19:00.100
With tens of thousands of Communist soldiers attacking us from both north and south,

468
19:00.100 --> 19:02.900
the Sichuan Army would be in for a world of trouble.

469
19:12.650 --> 19:15.650
Brother Yuanjing, what you said is absolutely right.

470
19:18.340 --> 19:19.740
Brother Yuanjing, come.

471
19:21.280 --> 19:22.080
Chairman Liu.

472
19:22.150 --> 19:23.250
No need, no need, no need.

473
19:23.250 --> 19:23.860
Come, come, come.

474
19:23.860 --> 19:24.490
No need, no need, no need.

475
19:24.490 --> 19:24.730
Come.

476
19:24.730 --> 19:26.460
It's fine here. It's fine here.

477
19:26.680 --> 19:27.580
You're an honored guest.

478
19:27.580 --> 19:29.070
Why go to such trouble?

479
19:29.200 --> 19:30.400
How can I neglect you?

480
19:46.100 --> 19:46.970
Everyone.

481
19:47.620 --> 19:49.650
We absolutely cannot let Zhu and Mao's Communist army

482
19:49.650 --> 19:51.300
attack our doorstep.

483
19:51.730 --> 19:54.330
I've therefore made a decision:

484
19:54.620 --> 19:58.120
effective immediately, we'll establish the South Bank General Headquarters for the Suppression of the Communists.

485
19:58.120 --> 19:58.760
Zhongsan.

486
19:59.110 --> 19:59.760
Here!

487
19:59.820 --> 20:00.660
Commander-in-Chief.

488
20:00.660 --> 20:01.250
Yes!

489
20:01.560 --> 20:02.210
Yizhi.

490
20:02.540 --> 20:03.170
Here!

491
20:03.530 --> 20:04.330
Vanguard,

492
20:04.590 --> 20:05.930
we must take the initiative and strike first.

493
20:05.930 --> 20:09.100
Our goal is to wipe out Zhu and Mao's Communist army before they can enter Sichuan.

494
20:09.100 --> 20:10.960
Not a single one of them will be allowed

495
20:10.960 --> 20:12.980
to set foot on Sichuan-Chongqing soil!

496
20:12.980 --> 20:14.130
Yes.

497
20:16.100 --> 20:17.100
Brother Fucheng,

498
20:17.540 --> 20:20.680
Generalissimo Chiang is having sleepless nights in Nanjing,

499
20:20.680 --> 20:22.810
waiting for these very words from you.

500
20:27.210 --> 20:28.900
Please rest assured, Commander-in-Chief.

501
20:28.900 --> 20:30.690
I will definitely not fail the mission

502
20:30.690 --> 20:34.350
and will let Zhu and Mao's Red Army see what the Sichuan Army can do!

503
20:37.340 --> 20:38.170
Zhongsan,

504
20:39.490 --> 20:42.780
what do you think of what I just said at the meeting?

505
20:43.490 --> 20:46.060
Commander-in-Chief, you only told half the story.

506
20:44.600 --> 20:48.220
[Pan Wenhua Commander-in-Chief of the Sichuan Army's South Bank Campaign to Suppress the Communists]

507
20:46.930 --> 20:48.380
You held something back.

508
20:52.410 --> 20:53.340
What do you mean?

509
20:54.490 --> 20:55.750
Commander-in-Chief,

510
20:55.970 --> 20:59.800
only by keeping the obvious threat out of Sichuan

511
21:00.150 --> 21:01.300
can we prevent

512
21:01.410 --> 21:03.340
the hidden threat from getting in.

513
21:03.340 --> 21:04.860
I've heard for a long time

514
21:05.640 --> 21:08.170
that after He Guoguang arrived in Chongqing,

515
21:08.410 --> 21:09.980
he hasn't been idle for a single day.

516
21:09.980 --> 21:12.170
He's been meeting with political figures from all walks of life everywhere,

517
21:12.170 --> 21:14.230
especially within the Sichuan Army.

518
21:14.320 --> 21:16.110
Many brigade and division commanders

519
21:16.110 --> 21:17.790
have been guests at his table.

520
21:18.580 --> 21:19.010
And...

521
21:22.980 --> 21:23.590
Who is it?

522
21:28.790 --> 21:30.920
Zhongsan, what are you nervous about?

523
21:31.410 --> 21:33.060
I know your character best.

524
21:41.100 --> 21:43.490
Among the many generals of the Sichuan Army,

525
21:43.490 --> 21:46.420
you are the one who understands things most clearly.

526
21:48.620 --> 21:51.490
This Chiang is truly hateful.

527
21:51.900 --> 21:53.700
With the situation as dire as it is,

528
21:53.700 --> 21:55.970
he still has the mind to pit one side against another

529
21:55.970 --> 21:57.900
and pull such underhanded tricks.

530
22:01.860 --> 22:03.410
I've told you before

531
22:04.500 --> 22:05.900
what kind of man Chiang Kai-shek is.

532
22:05.900 --> 22:07.620
No matter how sweetly he talks

533
22:07.860 --> 22:09.720
or how readily he makes promises,

534
22:10.250 --> 22:11.780
you must never trust him.

535
22:12.540 --> 22:13.870
We must unite with those

536
22:13.970 --> 22:16.970
forces from all sides whose interests are tied to ours

537
22:18.060 --> 22:19.410
to deal with him.

538
22:20.380 --> 22:22.580
Only then will there be a way to survive.

539
22:23.010 --> 22:23.940
I understand.

540
22:24.620 --> 22:25.950
The war on the South Bank

541
22:27.430 --> 22:29.190
also requires careful timing.

542
22:30.300 --> 22:31.140
Commander.

543
22:32.150 --> 22:33.310
Do you mean...

544
22:33.490 --> 22:36.550
If Zhu and Mao's Communist army insists on going north,

545
22:36.730 --> 22:39.410
we must fight them to the death.

546
22:40.020 --> 22:41.980
If they have another way to go,

547
22:42.410 --> 22:45.060
we might as well go with the flow.

548
22:48.790 --> 22:50.350
Understood.

549
22:52.650 --> 22:54.580
After the Red Army captured Zunyi,

550
22:54.690 --> 22:57.010
Chiang Kai-shek concentrated about 400,000 troops

551
22:57.010 --> 22:58.970
and pressed toward the Zunyi area,

552
22:59.250 --> 23:00.900
attempting to encircle and annihilate the Central Red Army

553
23:00.900 --> 23:04.170
in the region northwest of the Wujiang River, along the Sichuan-Guizhou border.

554
23:04.170 --> 23:05.900
Under these grave circumstances,

555
23:05.900 --> 23:08.580
on January 19, 1935,

556
23:08.610 --> 23:10.860
the Central Red Army withdrew from Zunyi

557
23:10.860 --> 23:13.380
and advanced toward Tucheng and Chishui,

558
23:13.580 --> 23:16.860
seeking a chance to cross the Yangtze River northward between Luzhou and Yibin.

559
23:16.860 --> 23:18.800
We Red Army troops are about to pull out!

560
23:18.800 --> 23:20.540
If any of you still hold Soviet currency,

561
23:20.540 --> 23:22.070
hurry to our exchange point

562
23:22.300 --> 23:24.060
and swap it for silver dollars, salt,

563
23:24.060 --> 23:25.490
or cloth!

564
23:26.010 --> 23:27.690
Fellow villagers, come on over!

565
23:27.690 --> 23:28.580
Don't rush.

566
23:29.380 --> 23:30.450
Form an orderly line.

567
23:30.450 --> 23:33.410
We guarantee a full exchange.

568
23:34.010 --> 23:37.380
We won't short anyone a single cent.

569
23:37.580 --> 23:38.600
One at a time.

570
23:38.900 --> 23:40.540
And goods are accepted for exchange too!

571
23:40.540 --> 23:42.820
Folks, there's enough for everyone.

572
23:43.540 --> 23:44.300
You can head over there

573
23:44.300 --> 23:45.210
to our exchange point.

574
23:45.210 --> 23:46.010
Fellow villager,

575
23:46.010 --> 23:47.930
you carry quite a lot of dampness in your body.

576
23:47.930 --> 23:49.650
Later,

577
23:50.060 --> 23:50.650
follow the prescription I wrote for you

578
23:50.650 --> 23:51.660
and pick up a dose of herbal medicine.

579
23:51.660 --> 23:54.370
[Yong Yuqin, Medic of the 3rd Red Army]

580
23:51.970 --> 23:52.340
That's it.

581
23:52.340 --> 23:53.860
Prescribe for me first. Prescribe me a box of medicine.

582
23:53.860 --> 23:54.270
Fellow villagers,

583
23:54.270 --> 23:55.640
don't worry, one by one.

584
23:55.780 --> 23:56.860
Come on. Next.

585
23:59.760 --> 24:00.690
Your pulse is relatively weak.

586
24:00.690 --> 24:02.900
I'll give you a dose of herbal medicine later.

587
24:02.900 --> 24:03.540
Fellow villagers,

588
24:03.540 --> 24:04.410
don't worry.

589
24:04.860 --> 24:05.920
One by one, please.

590
24:06.100 --> 24:08.030
I will see all of you before I leave.

591
24:12.900 --> 24:13.700
Leave it to me.

592
24:13.730 --> 24:14.970
I've been busy in the shop.

593
24:14.970 --> 24:16.210
Where have you been?

594
24:16.860 --> 24:18.410
I heard early this morning that they were leaving,

595
24:18.410 --> 24:19.580
and it got me worried,

596
24:19.580 --> 24:20.630
so I ran out to look.

597
24:20.630 --> 24:22.250
And there they were, paying out real gold and silver,

598
24:22.250 --> 24:24.340
refusing to short the common folk by so much as a cent.

599
24:24.340 --> 24:25.100
You saw it?

600
24:25.170 --> 24:26.590
I saw it clearly.

601
24:27.250 --> 24:28.580
Tell me, in all this world,

602
24:28.580 --> 24:30.580
where would you find such a fine army?

603
24:30.580 --> 24:31.580
Watch the shop.

604
24:34.140 --> 24:35.740
There's still one more here.

605
24:38.060 --> 24:39.520
I won't exchange this one.

606
24:40.390 --> 24:41.730
I'll keep it as a souvenir.

607
24:41.730 --> 24:42.410
Okay.

608
24:46.200 --> 24:47.640
Which house is it?

609
24:48.010 --> 24:49.140
You've even forgotten

610
24:49.140 --> 24:49.970
what their front door looks like.

611
24:49.970 --> 24:50.860
Don't rush me.

612
24:51.900 --> 24:52.730
You really are a scatterbrain.

613
24:52.730 --> 24:55.460
I just remember it's a family that makes candles.

614
24:55.490 --> 24:57.930
You're always losing things left and right.

615
24:57.930 --> 24:59.620
If you'd returned it earlier, it would have been settled.

616
24:59.620 --> 25:00.250
You just can't remember!

617
25:00.250 --> 25:01.410
Stop nagging. I...

618
25:03.620 --> 25:04.900
If we're gonna miss the main force,

619
25:04.900 --> 25:06.410
just see how I deal with you!

620
25:06.410 --> 25:08.140
Sir, I finally found you.

621
25:08.580 --> 25:10.510
Young comrade, what's the matter?

622
25:10.540 --> 25:11.800
I'm sorry, sir.

623
25:12.300 --> 25:14.780
I borrowed this strainer from your house the day before yesterday,

624
25:14.780 --> 25:16.710
and forgot to return it when I left.

625
25:16.920 --> 25:18.160
It's not worth much.

626
25:18.650 --> 25:20.490
My family doesn't usually use it.

627
25:20.490 --> 25:21.140
You don't have to return it.

628
25:21.140 --> 25:22.490
No, sir. We must return it.

629
25:22.490 --> 25:23.350
Return it to him.

630
25:23.350 --> 25:25.110
Yes, sir. We have discipline.

631
25:25.380 --> 25:27.300
Whatever we borrow from the villagers must be returned.

632
25:27.300 --> 25:28.370
Please take it.

633
25:30.170 --> 25:31.030
Thank you, sir.

634
25:31.540 --> 25:32.300
-Thank you, sir. -Thank you, sir.

635
25:32.300 --> 25:33.170
You're welcome.

636
25:33.170 --> 25:35.630
Let's hurry and catch up with the main force.

637
25:38.100 --> 25:38.900
What is it now?

638
25:39.360 --> 25:42.290
I forgot to return the thimble I borrowed from the folks.

639
25:42.290 --> 25:43.780
Don't take a single needle or thread from the masses.

640
25:43.780 --> 25:44.910
Didn't you say that?

641
25:45.240 --> 25:46.840
You're always so forgetful,

642
25:46.850 --> 25:49.540
borrowing things from the folks and not returning them!

643
25:49.540 --> 25:50.900
If I hadn't borrowed that thimble from the villager,

644
25:50.900 --> 25:53.030
how could I have sewn your underwears?

645
26:11.830 --> 26:14.580
[Wei Yueqiao, Staff of the 2nd Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

646
26:18.860 --> 26:20.450
Remember to apply this medicine

647
26:20.450 --> 26:21.540
to your wound.

648
26:22.040 --> 26:23.000
Whatever you do, don't let it get wet.

649
26:23.000 --> 26:24.200
Apply it 3 times a day.

650
26:24.580 --> 26:25.490
Okay.

651
26:29.300 --> 26:31.250
Are you bodhisattvas who treat illness for free?

652
26:31.250 --> 26:32.250
We are not bodhisattvas.

653
26:32.250 --> 26:33.910
We are doctors of the Red Army.

654
26:34.340 --> 26:35.380
Please save my dad!

655
26:35.380 --> 26:37.170
Please, save my dad!

656
26:37.170 --> 26:37.900
Young man,

657
26:37.900 --> 26:39.070
get up, young man.

658
26:39.730 --> 26:40.730
What's wrong with your dad?

659
26:40.730 --> 26:42.140
My dad is seriously ill.

660
26:42.340 --> 26:43.780
His body is burning hot,

661
26:44.100 --> 26:45.300
and his belly is swollen, round and tight.

662
26:45.300 --> 26:46.550
The pain has him writhing.

663
26:46.550 --> 26:47.310
Tell me,

664
26:47.450 --> 26:48.860
how many people in the village

665
26:48.860 --> 26:50.310
have symptoms like your dad's?

666
26:50.310 --> 26:51.630
There must be 30 or 40.

667
26:51.730 --> 26:53.170
A few have been died.

668
26:53.340 --> 26:54.340
Where do you live?

669
26:54.650 --> 26:55.860
I'm from Sangmuya.

670
26:55.860 --> 26:57.370
It's 20 li of mountain road from here.

671
26:57.370 --> 26:59.270
[He Cheng, Director of the General Health Department, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

672
26:57.480 --> 26:59.450
I heard from the folks who went to town to sell herbs

673
26:59.450 --> 27:01.250
that there were bodhisattva soldiers who treat people for free,

674
27:01.250 --> 27:02.410
so I hurried here.

675
27:02.410 --> 27:03.820
Please help save my dad.

676
27:03.990 --> 27:04.680
I beg you!

677
27:05.210 --> 27:05.940
Minister He,

678
27:06.060 --> 27:07.380
from what he describes,

679
27:07.380 --> 27:09.380
I think the village has most likely come down with typhoid—

680
27:09.380 --> 27:11.170
commonly called "chicken-coop fever."

681
27:11.170 --> 27:12.060
Let me go there.

682
27:13.900 --> 27:15.730
The main force is about to move out.

683
27:15.730 --> 27:17.460
I'm afraid time won't allow it.

684
27:19.900 --> 27:21.100
Living bodhisattvas,

685
27:21.100 --> 27:22.010
please save my dad.

686
27:22.010 --> 27:22.610
Young man.

687
27:22.780 --> 27:23.380
Young man.

688
27:23.380 --> 27:24.380
Please save my dad.

689
27:24.380 --> 27:24.820
Young man.

690
27:24.820 --> 27:25.540
Save my dad, please.

691
27:25.540 --> 27:26.270
Don't worry.

692
27:26.410 --> 27:27.540
I will save your dad.

693
27:27.780 --> 27:28.500
Minister He,

694
27:28.500 --> 27:30.420
tell me the direction the main force is heading.

695
27:30.420 --> 27:31.250
Once I finish treating the sick,

696
27:31.250 --> 27:32.510
I'll catch up with you.

697
27:34.060 --> 27:35.690
After leaving the city,

698
27:35.930 --> 27:37.450
the main force will head toward Tucheng.

699
27:37.450 --> 27:38.540
Okay, got it.

700
27:40.730 --> 27:41.780
Stay safe!

701
27:43.380 --> 27:44.730
Young man, let's go.

702
27:46.860 --> 27:47.450
Long,

703
27:48.900 --> 27:50.860
the enemy's pursuers will be here soon.

704
27:50.860 --> 27:52.010
You must not delay.

705
27:52.730 --> 27:53.780
Once you've seen the patients,

706
27:53.780 --> 27:55.540
come right away and catch up with the main force.

707
27:55.540 --> 27:56.870
We'll be waiting for you up ahead.

708
27:56.870 --> 27:57.600
Don't worry.

709
27:57.770 --> 27:58.270
I'm off!

710
27:58.850 --> 27:59.560
Stay safe!

711
28:04.340 --> 28:04.800
Take it.

712
28:04.860 --> 28:05.790
Come on. Take it.

713
28:05.900 --> 28:06.300
No need.

714
28:06.300 --> 28:06.860
Take it. Quick.

715
28:06.860 --> 28:07.650
We have discipline.

716
28:07.650 --> 28:07.970
We truly can't take it.

717
28:07.970 --> 28:08.540
Come on, take it.

718
28:08.540 --> 28:09.300
We really can't take it.

719
28:09.300 --> 28:09.900
We have discipline.

720
28:09.900 --> 28:10.820
We really can't take it.

721
28:10.820 --> 28:11.730
Eat it on the way.

722
28:11.730 --> 28:12.580
Keep some for yourself.

723
28:12.580 --> 28:13.690
It's just a little something.

724
28:13.690 --> 28:14.580
Just take it.

725
28:15.690 --> 28:16.820
It's homemade.

726
28:16.850 --> 28:17.730
We really can't accept it.

727
28:17.730 --> 28:18.620
Comrade.

728
28:18.750 --> 28:20.780
We have discipline. We can't take it.

729
28:20.780 --> 28:22.250
Comrade, take it.

730
28:22.340 --> 28:23.230
Take it.

731
28:25.690 --> 28:26.380
Lin Biao!

732
28:26.600 --> 28:27.790
Comrade Lin Biao.

733
28:28.490 --> 28:29.550
Hi, Commander Lin!

734
28:31.000 --> 28:34.960
I'd like to stay with the 1st Red Army Corps for a while

735
28:35.490 --> 28:38.820
to understand the particularities of China's civil war.

736
28:39.020 --> 28:40.020
The advisor said

737
28:40.040 --> 28:41.750
he'd like to stay with the 1st Red Army Corps for a while,

738
28:41.750 --> 28:42.730
so as to understand at the front

739
28:42.730 --> 28:44.330
the particularities of Chinese warfare

740
28:44.330 --> 28:46.020
that Chairman Mao spoke of.

741
28:46.420 --> 28:47.090
Really?

742
28:47.780 --> 28:50.170
Does Chairman Mao know about it?

743
28:50.200 --> 28:52.130
Does Chairman Mao know about this?

744
28:52.590 --> 28:54.500
Of course he does.

745
28:54.520 --> 28:55.000
Yes,

746
28:55.030 --> 28:57.170
he got permission from Comrade Mao Zedong.

747
28:57.170 --> 28:58.210
Comrade Lin Biao,

748
28:58.210 --> 29:00.440
I've read your "On Short, Swift Assaults."

749
29:00.440 --> 29:02.150
I found it very interesting,

750
29:02.650 --> 29:04.450
and I'd like to discuss the key questions

751
29:04.450 --> 29:08.170
raised in it with you.

752
29:08.510 --> 29:09.480
Comrade Advisor says

753
29:09.480 --> 29:11.550
he's read your "On Short, Swift Assaults."

754
29:11.550 --> 29:12.810
It's very well written.

755
29:12.810 --> 29:13.930
He'd like to spend some time

756
29:13.930 --> 29:15.690
discussing it with you in earnest.

757
29:15.690 --> 29:17.020
Where were you earlier?

758
29:18.170 --> 29:19.100
What did he say?

759
29:21.820 --> 29:22.620
He said "yes."

760
29:23.170 --> 29:25.860
Come with me to the Army Corps headquarters to report in.

761
29:25.860 --> 29:26.860
Go with him.

762
29:36.590 --> 29:39.120
[Chen Geng, head of the Cadre Regiment of the 1st Military Commission Column]

763
29:38.550 --> 29:39.240
Report.

764
29:39.410 --> 29:40.140
Come in.

765
29:41.100 --> 29:42.830
Hi, Political Commissar Chen.

766
29:43.210 --> 29:44.130
Hi, Comrade Chen Geng.

767
29:44.130 --> 29:45.590
Come in. Sit down, please.

768
29:48.900 --> 29:50.730
Is there any urgent task?

769
29:55.420 --> 29:56.620
Today, in my capacity

770
29:56.790 --> 29:59.540
as a Standing Committee member of the Central Politburo,

771
29:59.540 --> 30:01.380
political commissar of the Military Commission Column,

772
30:01.380 --> 30:04.640
and political commissar of the Zunyi Garrison Command,

773
30:04.770 --> 30:07.780
[Chen Yun, Member of the Standing Committee of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee and Political Commissar of the Military Commission Column]

774
30:05.110 --> 30:08.370
I'm speaking with you on behalf of the Party organization.

775
30:15.210 --> 30:15.900
Okay.

776
30:16.860 --> 30:17.970
Concerning your arrest

777
30:17.970 --> 30:20.690
between March and May of 1933:

778
30:20.900 --> 30:22.230
after a rigorous review

779
30:22.380 --> 30:24.620
by the Party organization,

780
30:25.340 --> 30:27.730
the findings are now out.

781
30:28.860 --> 30:31.320
It is confirmed that during your imprisonment,

782
30:31.320 --> 30:32.650
you withstood the test

783
30:32.970 --> 30:34.410
and committed no act

784
30:34.410 --> 30:37.210
that violated Party organizational discipline.

785
30:37.580 --> 30:40.030
The Party organization has decided that,

786
30:40.490 --> 30:41.490
effective today,

787
30:41.880 --> 30:45.270
your Party membership is formally restored.

788
30:45.830 --> 30:47.960
Congratulations, Comrade Chen Geng.

789
30:54.340 --> 30:55.290
I'm thirsty.

790
30:56.340 --> 30:58.200
Here's water. Please drink some.

791
31:04.970 --> 31:05.970
Slow down.

792
31:18.820 --> 31:19.580
I'm...

793
31:22.080 --> 31:23.080
still thirsty.

794
31:51.690 --> 31:52.580
I understand.

795
31:53.860 --> 31:55.990
Thank you, Political Commissar Chen.

796
32:00.100 --> 32:02.320
Please sit down.

797
32:06.530 --> 32:07.800
I'm not...

798
32:08.580 --> 32:09.380
Here you are.

799
32:10.250 --> 32:11.690
I'm not crying.

800
32:11.690 --> 32:13.600
These are

801
32:14.270 --> 32:15.710
tears of joy.

802
32:17.210 --> 32:18.100
I'm...

803
32:19.250 --> 32:20.450
I'm feeling happy.

804
32:21.300 --> 32:22.560
You're not the only one

805
32:23.180 --> 32:24.980
who is happy, Comrade Chen Geng.

806
32:25.620 --> 32:27.170
I'm happy too.

807
32:27.650 --> 32:28.450
You know what?

808
32:28.850 --> 32:30.370
After the Zunyi Conference,

809
32:30.370 --> 32:32.020
many comrades are happy

810
32:32.050 --> 32:33.250
and feel relieved.

811
32:33.500 --> 32:34.600
Especially Comrade Xiao Jinguang

812
32:34.600 --> 32:35.800
of your Cadre Regiment.

813
32:35.800 --> 32:37.210
His Party membership was restored immediately,

814
32:37.210 --> 32:38.590
along with his military status.

815
32:38.590 --> 32:41.520
And Luo Ming, Fang Qiang,

816
32:41.820 --> 32:43.150
and many other comrades

817
32:43.250 --> 32:44.860
will soon have their policies implemented

818
32:44.860 --> 32:45.920
and return to work.

819
32:46.620 --> 32:47.650
Comrades all say:

820
32:48.570 --> 32:49.390
once this meeting was over,

821
32:49.390 --> 32:51.250
things are really different now.

822
33:00.730 --> 33:02.060
I'm not crying anymore.

823
33:02.580 --> 33:03.580
I thank the Party.

824
33:03.730 --> 33:05.130
I thank Comrade Chen Yun.

825
33:05.650 --> 33:06.620
Later,

826
33:07.620 --> 33:09.730
I'll go find Xiao Jinguang

827
33:10.820 --> 33:11.900
and cry our eyes out

828
33:13.510 --> 33:14.710
in each other's arms.

829
33:25.010 --> 33:26.960
According to the order of the Military Commission,

830
33:26.960 --> 33:29.960
all army corps have completed their reorganization.

831
33:29.990 --> 33:30.780
After the reorganization,

832
33:30.780 --> 33:32.630
the 1st Army Corps has been reduced to 2 divisions.

833
33:32.630 --> 33:33.820
The former 15th Division has been merged

834
33:33.820 --> 33:35.430
into the 1st and 2nd Divisions.

835
33:35.430 --> 33:36.930
The 3rd Red Army Corps has been reduced to 2 divisions

836
33:36.930 --> 33:37.930
plus one independent regiment,

837
33:37.930 --> 33:39.650
and the designation of the 6th Division has been abolished.

838
33:39.650 --> 33:41.250
The 5th and 9th Red Army Corps

839
33:41.480 --> 33:43.180
have abolished their division designations

840
33:43.180 --> 33:44.110
and now command

841
33:44.140 --> 33:46.780
the 37th, 38th, and 39th Regiments

842
33:47.410 --> 33:49.210
and the 7th, 8th, and 9th Regiments, respectively.

843
33:49.210 --> 33:49.820
Good.

844
33:50.110 --> 33:51.870
After the reorganization, the troops are leaner

845
33:51.870 --> 33:53.460
and more agile in battle.

846
33:53.490 --> 33:54.170
Report.

847
33:56.060 --> 33:57.100
Comrade Kaixiang!

848
33:57.000 --> 33:59.480
[Huang Kaixiang, Political Commissar of the 22nd Division, 9th Red Army Corps]

849
33:57.900 --> 33:59.030
Vice Chairman Zhou,

850
33:59.820 --> 34:00.540
I'm here.

851
34:00.970 --> 34:02.490
Chairman Mao, you are here too.

852
34:02.490 --> 34:03.450
Comrade Kaixiang,

853
34:03.450 --> 34:05.620
it's been over half a year since we parted at Huichang.

854
34:05.620 --> 34:07.150
Yeah, more than half a year!

855
34:08.010 --> 34:09.810
My respects to you both, Chiefs.

856
34:10.040 --> 34:10.860
Comrade Kaixiang.

857
34:10.860 --> 34:12.989
Greetings, Commander-in-Chief Zhu!

858
34:13.380 --> 34:14.239
Good to see you.

859
34:14.960 --> 34:15.739
Comrade Kaixiang.

860
34:15.739 --> 34:16.300
Here!

861
34:16.449 --> 34:18.610
We specifically transferred you from the 9th Red Army Corps

862
34:18.610 --> 34:20.570
this time because there's an important task,

863
34:20.570 --> 34:22.429
and we want to hear your thoughts.

864
34:23.090 --> 34:25.350
Vice Chairman Zhou, just give the order.

865
34:25.969 --> 34:28.409
Comrade Geng Biao,

866
34:28.739 --> 34:31.010
is being transferred to the 1st Division as its chief of staff.

867
34:31.010 --> 34:31.900
The Military Commission has decided to ask you

868
34:31.900 --> 34:34.230
to serve as commander of the 4th Regiment.

869
34:34.340 --> 34:37.050
But considering you are a division-level cadre,

870
34:37.050 --> 34:38.050
this means...

871
34:40.570 --> 34:42.300
Vice Chairman Zhou, say no more.

872
34:42.300 --> 34:43.219
I understand.

873
34:43.310 --> 34:45.900
You're worried I might have misgivings, aren't you?

874
34:45.900 --> 34:47.360
Rest assured, I have none.

875
34:47.610 --> 34:48.929
I firmly obey the order,

876
34:48.929 --> 34:51.179
and I guarantee I won't have any other thoughts

877
34:51.179 --> 34:52.929
about it whatsoever. Really.

878
34:54.610 --> 34:56.170
I'd prepared a bellyful of words

879
34:56.170 --> 34:57.660
to do your ideological work,

880
34:57.660 --> 34:58.650
and with that one sentence,

881
34:58.650 --> 35:00.780
you've left me with no room to use them!

882
35:02.530 --> 35:03.180
Leaders,

883
35:03.610 --> 35:04.740
to be frank with you,

884
35:04.860 --> 35:07.450
I, Huang Kaixiang, am nothing more than a barrel cooper.

885
35:07.450 --> 35:08.740
If I hadn't been making revolution

886
35:08.740 --> 35:10.870
under Chairman Fang Zhimin back then,

887
35:10.940 --> 35:13.350
I'd still be making barrels in Yiyang today.

888
35:13.350 --> 35:15.570
But Chairman Fang once told me:

889
35:15.790 --> 35:17.190
our revolutionary ranks

890
35:17.860 --> 35:19.190
are like a water bucket.

891
35:19.540 --> 35:21.060
Every stave

892
35:21.080 --> 35:23.610
must be bound tightly together, edge to edge,

893
35:23.610 --> 35:25.010
or the water will leak.

894
35:25.340 --> 35:27.090
So whatever the revolution asks of me,

895
35:27.090 --> 35:28.930
I'll do it for sure.

896
35:30.260 --> 35:31.090
Comrade Kaixiang.

897
35:31.090 --> 35:31.610
Here.

898
35:31.700 --> 35:33.660
Comrade Geng Biao is still in Zunyi.

899
35:33.660 --> 35:34.660
We will notify him

900
35:35.060 --> 35:36.780
to hand over his duties to you on the spot.

901
35:36.780 --> 35:38.570
The two of you

902
35:38.700 --> 35:40.130
should report to your new posts as soon as possible.

903
35:40.130 --> 35:40.930
Yes, sir.

904
35:41.260 --> 35:42.130
Comrade Kaixiang.

905
35:42.130 --> 35:42.660
Here.

906
35:43.050 --> 35:45.490
The 4th Regiment is the vanguard regiment of the whole army.

907
35:45.490 --> 35:46.820
You, the "Axe General,"

908
35:46.860 --> 35:48.660
are taking office as its vanguard commander.

909
35:48.660 --> 35:50.590
There are many hard battles ahead.

910
35:51.050 --> 35:52.450
You must dare to charge and fight,

911
35:52.450 --> 35:54.180
but you must also use your wits.

912
35:54.340 --> 35:56.340
Chairman Mao, please rest assured.

913
35:56.540 --> 35:58.090
At Huichang, you told me 8 words,

914
35:58.090 --> 35:59.260
and I've kept them all:

915
35:59.260 --> 36:00.820
"Be flexible and mobile!"

916
36:05.190 --> 36:07.790
It bothers me that you left out the last 4 words.

917
36:09.940 --> 36:13.690
"Stay mobile and flexible. Destroy the enemy on the move." Right?

918
36:14.450 --> 36:16.850
Those eight words are still just as useful.

919
36:17.090 --> 36:18.820
I await your report of victory.

920
36:18.860 --> 36:19.480
Yes, sir!

921
36:24.780 --> 36:26.500
We must thank Comrade Fang Zhimin

922
36:26.500 --> 36:28.220
for training such a fine cadre,

923
36:28.220 --> 36:31.080
excellent in both military and political affairs.

924
36:31.090 --> 36:33.020
I wonder how the 10th Red Army Corps

925
36:33.340 --> 36:34.590
is faring now.

926
36:44.430 --> 36:51.110
[Songkan, Zunyi, Guizhou Encampment of the 4th Red Army]

927
36:45.080 --> 36:46.210
Reluctant to leave?

928
36:46.410 --> 36:47.140
To be honest,

929
36:47.490 --> 36:48.130
yes.

930
36:49.410 --> 36:51.610
I've been with the 4th Regiment for nearly 2 years.

931
36:51.610 --> 36:52.530
We fought

932
36:53.220 --> 36:54.610
so many hard,

933
36:54.780 --> 36:56.240
bitter battles together.

934
36:56.410 --> 36:57.810
It feels like yesterday.

935
36:58.780 --> 37:00.340
Sometimes I think back...

936
37:00.950 --> 37:03.490
[Yang Chengwu, Political Commissar of the 4th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

937
37:02.250 --> 37:03.650
Think back to what?

938
37:03.770 --> 37:07.190
[Geng Biao, Commander of the 4th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

939
37:06.090 --> 37:08.970
I remember when I first arrived at the 4th Regiment and learned

940
37:08.970 --> 37:12.340
the regimental political commissar was 5 years younger than me,

941
37:12.340 --> 37:14.180
I was really uneasy.

942
37:14.610 --> 37:15.930
And then?

943
37:16.260 --> 37:18.320
Do I even need to say how it turned out?

944
37:18.700 --> 37:21.450
Out of all the regiments in the Central Red Army,

945
37:22.050 --> 37:23.440
the pairing we have

946
37:24.380 --> 37:25.380
is second to none.

947
37:26.000 --> 37:27.400
From Jiangxi to Guizhou,

948
37:28.050 --> 37:30.130
we've fought side by side

949
37:30.430 --> 37:31.960
through the hardest times.

950
37:45.100 --> 37:46.160
Take this with you.

951
37:53.820 --> 37:56.220
It's the prize from the Tengtian Red Sports Meet.

952
37:56.220 --> 37:58.150
It's the only one our regiment has.

953
37:58.180 --> 38:00.310
The honor belongs to the 4th Regiment.

954
38:00.410 --> 38:01.610
Keep it as a keepsake.

955
38:04.350 --> 38:05.760
The new commander should be arriving soon.

956
38:05.760 --> 38:08.020
I'll go meet him at the village entrance.

957
38:37.610 --> 38:38.700
Give me the camera.

958
38:51.450 --> 38:52.180
Mao Zhenhua!

959
38:52.410 --> 38:53.340
Yes, Commander!

960
38:54.820 --> 38:55.930
Fight well.

961
38:57.240 --> 38:58.410
Observe discipline.

962
38:58.260 --> 39:01.380
[Mao Zhenhua, Company Commander of the 3rd Company, 1st Battalion, 4th Regiment]

963
38:58.820 --> 38:59.780
Obey orders.

964
39:00.220 --> 39:01.680
You can endure hardships,

965
39:01.700 --> 39:03.370
but you must not throw your weight around.

966
39:03.370 --> 39:04.290
If I hear

967
39:04.320 --> 39:06.130
you've been doing brutish things in the regiment,

968
39:06.130 --> 39:08.530
I'll come over from the 1st Division and kick you!

969
39:08.530 --> 39:09.210
Yes, sir.

970
40:10.090 --> 40:11.290
Regiment Commander.

971
40:12.130 --> 40:12.840
Look,

972
40:14.340 --> 40:16.670
I'm not the only one who hates to see you go.

973
40:16.930 --> 40:17.700
Regiment Commander.

974
40:17.700 --> 40:21.500
-Regiment Commander! -Regiment Commander! -Regiment Commander!

975
40:25.690 --> 40:26.890
Regiment Commander.

976
40:27.130 --> 40:28.490
Take this soap pod.

977
40:28.510 --> 40:29.110
Regiment Commander.

978
40:29.110 --> 40:30.020
Take them all.

979
40:30.220 --> 40:31.250
-Regiment Commander! -Regiment Commander!

980
40:31.250 --> 40:32.250
I don't need them.

981
40:32.630 --> 40:33.690
You guys keep them.

982
40:33.820 --> 40:34.380
Keep them.

983
40:34.380 --> 40:35.440
Take them, please.

984
40:35.530 --> 40:36.390
Follow orders!

985
40:42.890 --> 40:45.020
Regiment Commander, we will miss you.

986
40:57.180 --> 40:58.130
Comrades,

987
40:58.450 --> 41:01.180
let me introduce the new commander of our 4th Red Regiment,

988
41:01.180 --> 41:02.550
Comrade Huang Kaixiang!

989
41:02.550 --> 41:04.410
Let's welcome him with applause.

990
41:14.440 --> 41:15.210
Welcome.

991
41:17.430 --> 41:19.720
Well, you go ahead and say your goodbyes.

992
41:20.180 --> 41:22.980
I'll have the Political Commissar show me around.

993
41:23.300 --> 41:24.150
Go ahead.

994
41:24.760 --> 41:25.310
Okay.

995
41:25.340 --> 41:26.230
Geng,

996
41:26.930 --> 41:28.230
use that treasured camera of yours

997
41:28.230 --> 41:30.050
to take a picture with the comrades.

998
41:30.050 --> 41:30.670
Alright.

999
41:32.440 --> 41:33.700
Let me take one for you.

1000
41:34.340 --> 41:35.050
Okay.

1001
41:40.660 --> 41:41.570
This is the shutter.

1002
41:41.570 --> 41:42.690
Okay, no problem.

1003
41:42.820 --> 41:43.350
Go ahead.

1004
41:43.530 --> 41:44.660
Come on, get up here.

1005
41:45.490 --> 41:46.440
Come on, gather around for a picture.

1006
41:46.440 --> 41:47.700
Everyone, get up here.

1007
41:49.010 --> 41:49.820
The front row, squat down. Hurry.

1008
41:49.820 --> 41:51.090
Move forward. Hurry.

1009
41:55.410 --> 41:56.810
Comrades, close in a bit.

1010
41:58.180 --> 41:59.570
Come on, look at me.

1011
42:00.610 --> 42:01.840
Smile.

1012
42:19.010 --> 42:20.380
Seeing you all,

1013
42:20.600 --> 42:21.930
I'm reminded of the comrades of my 22nd Division

1014
42:21.930 --> 42:23.260
who saw me off.

1015
42:24.010 --> 42:25.870
They were every bit as reluctant,

1016
42:26.380 --> 42:27.640
faces stretched long,

1017
42:27.790 --> 42:29.020
just like you.

1018
42:29.490 --> 42:30.750
I didn't have a camera.

1019
42:31.220 --> 42:31.790
If I had,

1020
42:31.820 --> 42:32.920
I'd have taken a picture to show you.

1021
42:32.920 --> 42:34.410
It would have scared you to death.

1022
42:34.410 --> 42:36.410
Anyway, it scared the life out of me.

1023
42:36.450 --> 42:38.050
I thought I owed them 100 silver dollars I hadn't repaid,

1024
42:38.050 --> 42:39.180
and then I ran off.

1025
42:42.800 --> 42:43.950
No, not a hundred,

1026
42:44.410 --> 42:45.490
but three hundred.

1027
42:50.940 --> 42:53.340
While the Zunyi Conference was in session,

1028
42:53.680 --> 42:56.600
the 10th Red Army Corps

1029
42:56.630 --> 42:58.610
suffered repeated defeats after the Battle of Tanjiaqiao,

1030
42:58.610 --> 43:02.490
and was forced to withdraw southward from the Anhui–Jiangxi border
